# Findings

## High — The isolated OpenCode command still repeats the known failing containment check

Phase 2 still canonicalizes `oc_bin` with `realpath` and compares it to the non-canonical `oc_root`. On macOS, a temporary path reported under `/var/...` commonly canonicalizes under `/private/var/...`; a binary genuinely contained in the install therefore fails `case "$oc_bin" in "$oc_root"/node_modules/*)`. The retained Phase 1 result already records this prescribed check aborting the exact isolated OpenCode attempt, so the unchanged command cannot reliably reach the required mixed-host certification.

Canonicalize `oc_root` or `oc_root/node_modules` before the containment comparison, and use that canonical boundary consistently for the exact-version launch and guarded cleanup while continuing to reject a binary that genuinely escapes the install.

## Medium — The debris check still cannot detect Unix sockets

Phase 1 still runs `find packages -type f (...)` while claiming to exclude `*.sock` debris. Unix socket nodes are not regular files, so this assertion cannot detect them. Remove the blanket `-type f` restriction or add a separate socket-node check so the verify command covers the stated acceptance criterion.
